[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:94. Future Champions]
[00:00.520]Passage 94 | 文章九十四
[00:02.840]Future Champions. | 未来冠军。
[00:05.505]Experiments have proved that children can be instructed in swimming | 实验证明，儿童可以在很小的年纪
[00:10.805]at a very early age. | 就学会游泳。
[00:13.165]At a special swimming pool in Los Angeles, | 在洛杉矶的一个特殊游泳池里，
[00:16.710]children become expert at holding their breath underwater | 孩子们甚至在能走路之前，
[00:20.860]even before they can walk. | 就能熟练地在水下屏住呼吸。
[00:23.460]Babies of two months old | 两个月大的婴儿
[00:26.305]do not appear to be reluctant to enter the water. | 似乎并不排斥入水。
[00:29.970]It is not long before they are so accustomed to swimming | 不久之后，他们就非常习惯游泳了，
[00:34.385]that they can pick up weights from the floor of the pool. | 甚至能从池底捡起重物。
[00:38.950]A game that is very popular with these young swimmers | 一项深受这些小泳者欢迎的游戏
[00:43.245]is the underwater tricycle race. | 是水下三轮车比赛。
[00:46.790]Tricycles are lined up on the floor of the pool, | 三轮车排成一排，放在
[00:51.055]seven feet underwater. | 水下七英尺深的池底。
[00:53.515]The children compete against each other | 孩子们互相竞争，
[00:56.900]to reach the other end of the pool. | 看谁能先到达泳池的另一端。
[00:59.725]Many pedal their tricycles, | 许多人蹬三轮车，
[01:02.755]but most of them prefer to push or drag them. | 但大多数人更喜欢推或拖着它们。
[01:06.555]Some children can cover the whole length of the pool | 有些孩子甚至不用浮出水面换气一次，
[01:10.630]without coming up for breath even once. | 就能游完整个泳池的长度。
[01:14.390]Whether they will ever become future Olympic champions, | 他们将来是否会成为奥运冠军，
[01:18.795]only time will tell. | 只有时间才能告诉我们。
[01:21.040]Meanwhile, they should encourage those among us | 同时，他们应该鼓励我们中那些
[01:24.940]who cannot swim five yards | 游不到五码
[01:27.450]before they are gasping for air. | 就气喘吁吁的人。